            <mo>∗<!-- ∗ --></mo>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle f_{*}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/903e97c260c5d157bff320b5e38e0e4b42cd20ad" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.671ex; width:2.193ex; height:2.509ex;" alt="{\displaystyle f_{*}}"/></span>.</p>

<p id="mwWQ">This map exists without any assumptions on the maps <i id="mwWg">f</i> and <i id="mwWw">g</i>. It is constructed as follows: since <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt33" id="mwXA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"g&apos;^*"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle g'^{*}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mi>g</mi>
          <mrow>
            <mo class="MJX-variant">′</mo>
            <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
              <mo>∗<!-- ∗ --></mo>
            </mrow>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle g'^{*}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/550ee90454312332b54baf8e56435cfc5ca2a4c7" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.671ex; width:2.625ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle g'^{*}}"/></span> is <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adjoint_functor" title="Adjoint functor" class="mw-redirect" id="mwXQ">left adjoint</a> to <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt34" id="mwXg" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"g&apos;_*"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle g'_{*}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msubsup>
          <mi>g</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mo>∗<!-- ∗ --></mo>
          </mrow>
          <mo>′</mo>
        </msubsup>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle g'_{*}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/25c40328fab92d64ff3fa97f80c8d4f9922dea8f" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.671ex; width:2.163ex; height:2.509ex;" alt="{\displaystyle g'_{*}}"/></span>, there is a natural map (called unit map)</p>
<dl id="mwXw"><dd id="mwYA"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt35" id="mwYQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\operatorname{id} \\to g&apos;_* \\circ g&apos;^*"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \operatorname {id} \to g'_{*}\circ g'^{*}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
