</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/bc9dd879d0c8588bca8875b13721493d46a9c4c1" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.671ex; width:23.301ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle R^{r}f_{*}\to R^{r}f_{*}\circ g'_{*}\circ g'^{*}.}"/></span></dd></dl>

<p id="mwZg">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grothendieck_spectral_sequence" title="Grothendieck spectral sequence" id="mwZw">Grothendieck spectral sequence</a> then gives the first map and the last map (they are edge maps) in:</p>

<dl id="mwaA"><dd id="mwaQ"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt37" id="mwag" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"R^r f_* \\circ g&apos;_* \\circ g&apos;^* \\to R^r(f \\circ g&apos;)_* \\circ g&apos;^* = R^r(g \\circ f&apos;)_* \\circ g&apos;^* \\to g_* \\circ R^r f&apos;_* \\circ g&apos;^*."}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle R^{r}f_{*}\circ g'_{*}\circ g'^{*}\to R^{r}(f\circ g')_{*}\circ g'^{*}=R^{r}(g\circ f')_{*}\circ g'^{*}\to g_{*}\circ R^{r}f'_{*}\circ g'^{*}.}">
  <semantics>
