<p id="mwnw">To encode all individual higher derived functors of <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt57" id="mwoA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"f_*"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle f_{*}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msub>
          <mi>f</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mo>∗<!-- ∗ --></mo>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle f_{*}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/903e97c260c5d157bff320b5e38e0e4b42cd20ad" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.671ex; width:2.193ex; height:2.509ex;" alt="{\displaystyle f_{*}}"/></span> into one entity, the above statement may equivalently be rephrased by saying that the base change map</p>

<dl id="mwoQ"><dd id="mwog"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt58" id="mwow" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"g^* Rf_* \\mathcal F \\to Rf&apos;_* g&apos;^* \\mathcal F"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle g^{*}Rf_{*}{\mathcal {F}}\to Rf'_{*}g'^{*}{\mathcal {F}}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mi>g</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mo>∗<!-- ∗ --></mo>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <mi>R</mi>
        <msub>
          <mi>f</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mo>∗<!-- ∗ --></mo>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi class="MJX-tex-caligraphic" mathvariant="script">F</mi>
          </mrow>
        </mrow>
        <mo stretchy="false">→<!-- → --></mo>
        <mi>R</mi>
        <msubsup>
          <mi>f</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mo>∗<!-- ∗ --></mo>
          </mrow>
          <mo>′</mo>
        </msubsup>
        <msup>
          <mi>g</mi>
          <mrow>
            <mo class="MJX-variant">′</mo>
            <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
              <mo>∗<!-- ∗ --></mo>
            </mrow>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi class="MJX-tex-caligraphic" mathvariant="script">F</mi>
          </mrow>
        </mrow>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle g^{*}Rf_{*}{\mathcal {F}}\to Rf'_{*}g'^{*}{\mathcal {F}}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/dc60a159e6da158ea913b53ce76431b0260f678b" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.671ex; width:20.18ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle g^{*}Rf_{*}{\mathcal {F}}\to Rf'_{*}g'^{*}{\mathcal {F}}}"/></span></dd></dl>

<p id="mwpA">is a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quasi-isomorphism" title="Quasi-isomorphism" id="mwpQ">quasi-isomorphism</a>.</p>

<p id="mwpg">The assumptions that the involved spaces be Hausdorff have been weakened by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#CITEREFSchnürerSoergel2016" about="#mwt59" typeof="mw:Transclusion" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwpw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"harvtxt","href":"./Template:Harvtxt"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Schnürer"},"2":{"wt":"Soergel"},"3":{"wt":"2016"}},"i":0}}]}'>Schnürer <span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span> Soergel (2016)</a>.</p>

<p id="mwqA"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#CITEREFLurie2009" about="#mwt60" typeof="mw:Transclusion" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwqQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"harvtxt","href":"./Template:Harvtxt"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Lurie"},"2":{"wt":"2009"}},"i":0}}]}'>Lurie (2009)</a> has extended the above theorem to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Non-abelian_cohomology" title="Non-abelian cohomology" class="mw-redirect" id="mwqg">non-abelian sheaf cohomology</a>, i.e., sheaves taking values in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Simplicial_set" title="Simplicial set" id="mwqw">simplicial sets</a> (as opposed to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abelian_group" title="Abelian group" id="mwrA">abelian groups</a>).<sup about="#mwt62" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-3"}}'><a href="#cite_note-3" id="mwrQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwrg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwrw">[</span>3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwsA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="5" id="mwsQ" aria-labelledby="Direct_image_with_compact_support"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Direct_image_with_compact_support">Direct image with compact support</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Base_change_theorems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5" title="Edit section: Direct image with compact support"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwsg">If the map <i id="mwsw">f</i> is not closed, the base change map need not be an isomorphism, as the following example shows (the maps are the standard inclusions)<span typeof="mw:DisplaySpace" id="mwtA"> </span>:</p>

<dl id="mwtQ"><dd id="mwtg"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt63" id="mwtw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\begin{array}{rcl}\n\\emptyset &amp; \\stackrel {g&apos;} \\to &amp; \\mathbb C \\setminus \\{0\\} \\\\\nf&apos; \\downarrow &amp; &amp; \\downarrow f \\\\\n\\{0\\} &amp; \\stackrel g \\to &amp; \\mathbb C\n\\end{array}\n"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle {\begin{array}{rcl}\emptyset &amp;{\stackrel {g'}{\to }}&amp;\mathbb {C} \setminus \{0\}\\f'\downarrow &amp;&amp;\downarrow f\\\{0\}&amp;{\stackrel {g}{\to }}&amp;\mathbb {C} \end{array}}}">
  <semantics>
