</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/733ceec01030c7e2888bbe14a9de7a1913bdca56" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -1.171ex; width:6.723ex; height:3.009ex;" alt="{\displaystyle {\mathcal {O}}_{S,f(x)}}"/></span>). In this situation, the following statements hold:<sup about="#mwt88" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-5"}}'><a href="#cite_note-5" id="mw6g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw6w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw7A">[</span>5<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw7Q">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
<ul id="mw7g"><li id="mw7w">"Semicontinuity theorem":
<ul id="mw8A"><li id="mw8Q">For each <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt89" id="mw8g" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"p \\ge 0"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle p\geq 0}">
